From 1b809a8bb8212cd11aa367b7f67f14fee2213e65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler South <tsouth2@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:31:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 175/176] Wait for audio changes instead of polling pactl

The Windows audio bridge ran pactl get-default-sink and get-default-source
every quarter second, about 14 new PipeWire clients a second, which kept
QEMU, WirePlumber and PipeWire busy at idle. It now holds one pactl
subscribe and checks the defaults, volume and mute when a server, sink,
source or module event arrives, with a check every five seconds as a
safety net. A subscription that ends is restarted after a second, and
the check that follows catches what it missed. Compatibility revision 69
delivers the bridge to existing disks.
